         }
      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "CGI versions before 5.00 for Perl allow the POSTDATA, PUTDATA, PATCHDATA and XForms:Model parameters to be set from the query string or form fields.\n\nCGI stores a non-form request body under POSTDATA, PUTDATA or PATCHDATA, and an XForms body under XForms:Model, but also accepts these names from the query string, a form field or a multipart part, so an application cannot tell a client-sent value from the real body.\n\nA cross-site HTML form can post POSTDATA={\"admin\":true} to an endpoint that reads JSON from param('POSTDATA'), a request forgery that needs no CORS preflight.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
      "publisher": {
